# Chapter 2: Santeem's castle, Surene, Tempe, Frenor, the Birdsong Tower, the desert Bazaar, the shrine of the
# travel door and Endor (its colosseum is still to come).
# Their walls, grounds, plants and water are squares chapter 1's places have too (chapter1.map pairs them: a
# line for any kind of map serves here as well); this file pairs what is new in them. The inventories are the
# whole game's, one for each kind of map (the game's number at $28): nes_kXX.
# A thing the Super Famicom games have no picture of keeps its NES shape, laid over their real ground ("over ~");
# "=town:3E51A0A88427F85B" is the floor the place itself has (a town's road, a castle's floor, a room's).

lib dq3t ../../../generated/sfc/dq3_town.sfclib
